Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: the game's vibration reaches an XInput pad under Wine when XInputGetState does not report it

Under Proton (the Legion Go 2 in Steam's Game Mode) XInputGetState answered "not connected" for the pad Steam makes while XInputSetState on user 0 vibrated it (PS2X_XINPUT_TRACE=2 showed "ok"), so the game's vibration never reached the pad. Under Wine user 0 is now written to when no pad is found; a "not connected" answer lets go of it as before.

--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_xinput_rumble.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_xinput_rumble.cpp
@@ -128,6 +128,16 @@ namespace ps2x::xinput
         int64_t g_nextScan = 0;
         Speeds g_written;     // what the pad was last told (off: it is never touched before the game vibrates)
 
+        bool underWine()
+        {
+            static const bool wine = []()
+            {
+                const HMODULE ntdll = GetModuleHandleW(L"ntdll.dll");
+                return ntdll && GetProcAddress(ntdll, "wine_get_version") != nullptr;
+            }();
+            return wine;
+        }
+
         int firstConnectedUser()
         {
             for (DWORD i = 0; i < 4; ++i)
@@ -290,7 +300,10 @@ namespace ps2x::xinput
             g_user = firstConnectedUser();
             if (g_user < 0)
             {
-                if (!test)
+                // (Under Wine - Proton on Linux - XInputGetState can answer "not connected" for a pad that XInputSetState vibrates:
+                // user 0 is written to then, and write() lets go of it when that answers "not connected" too: the next scan is a
+                // second later.)
+                if (!test && !underWine())
                     return;
                 g_user = 0; // (the test mode's call to an empty slot)
             }
